WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Retrieval practice begins with an attempt to bring knowledge to mind.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.891
Ask for a short explanation before showing the answer.

3
00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:13.402
Then reveal corrective feedback and revisit the idea later with a changed example.

4
00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:21.111
QuizSplat can support questions, flashcards and team activities, but the learning depends on the prompt and the

5
00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:22.345
attempt.

6
00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:26.163
A learner copying a displayed answer is doing a different task.

7
00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:29.577
Build a five-item check tied to the module goal.

8
00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:35.438
Include two essential facts, two reasoning questions and one new-case application.

9
00:00:35.638 --> 00:00:39.367
Ask what an incorrect response would tell you to teach next.

10
00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:44.352
Avoid questions whose difficulty comes mainly from confusing wording.

11
00:00:44.552 --> 00:00:48.738
For flashcards, require an answer before turning the card over.

12
00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:53.413
For team play, let each learner commit a response before the discussion.

13
00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:56.585
Use the responses to plan the next action.

14
00:00:56.785 --> 00:01:01.381
Provide a short explanation when students need it, not just a mark.

15
00:01:01.581 --> 00:01:05.897
Schedule a later retrieval opportunity in PlanSplat or your calendar.

16
00:01:06.097 --> 00:01:11.263
A team score can make a review energetic but may hide an individual misconception.

17
00:01:11.463 --> 00:01:17.949
Pause and write one question that checks reasoning and one follow-up question using a different example.
